# Accepted gaps for 21-callable-function-members — each line is an edge the TypeScript
# compiler resolves and this engine does not. A NEW missing edge fails the suite; a line
# here that STARTS working also fails, so the debt cannot rot.
#
# Both are `const m = r.lookup; m.call(r, 'k')` — a METHOD REFERENCE stored in a const.
# The engine never establishes that `m` is callable, so `expr_callable` does not hold and
# the Function-members rule has no receiver to attach to. This is the untyped-receiver
# gap, not a Function-members gap: the same shape accounts for every remaining
# call/apply/bind miss measured on the corpus (13 CALL_RESULT, 6 PROPERTY_CHAIN, none
# carrying a receiver type). Fixing receiver typing closes these; adding member rules
# does not.
strict-bind#viaMethodReference(Registry) -> CallableFunction#bind(any,any)
strict-bind#viaMethodReference(Registry) -> CallableFunction#call(any,any,any)
